 ## Overview
-This method simultaneously optimizes the camera poses $P$ and the Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) parameters $\theta$ without requiring pre-estimated camera parameters [S1][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of reconstructing 3D scenes from sparse, forward-facing views where camera intrinsics and extrinsics are unknown [S2, unofficial]. Unlike baseline NeRF which relies on external Structure-from-Motion (SfM) pipelines like COLMAP, this approach eliminates the need for pre-estimated camera poses by treating them as learnable parameters [S2, unofficial]. It achieves novel view synthesis (NVS) quality comparable to baseline NeRF (with $\Delta$SSIM and $\Delta$LPIPS $\approx 0.05$) but requires no external pose estimation [S2, unofficial].
+This method simultaneously optimizes the camera poses $P$ and the Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) parameters $\theta$ without requiring pre-estimated camera parameters [S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of reconstructing 3D scenes from sparse, forward-facing views where camera intrinsics and extrinsics are unknown [S3, unofficial]. Unlike baseline NeRF which relies on external Structure-from-Motion (SfM) pipelines like COLMAP, this approach eliminates the need for pre-estimated camera poses by treating them as learnable parameters [S1, unofficial]. It achieves novel view synthesis (NVS) quality comparable to baseline NeRF (with $\Delta$SSIM and $\Delta$LPIPS $\approx 0.05$) but requires no external pose estimation [S3, unofficial].
 
